# No long dashes

Do not use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) anywhere in user-facing copy, metadata, comments, or UI strings.

## Prefer instead

- Short hyphen: `-` (ranges, compound words, empty placeholders)
- Comma, colon, full stop, or a new sentence for pauses

## Examples

```text
❌ Using example assumptions — adjust them to match your car.
✅ Using example assumptions. Adjust them to match your car.

❌ Estimates only — not live market data.
✅ Estimates only: not live market data.

❌ 12–36 months
✅ 12-36 months

❌ return "—"
✅ return "-"
```

Apply this in every project unless the user explicitly asks for typographic dashes.
